{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792791685,"nonce":"E8vn19bSJnOnJ+MwMA9aQfQSSOQ=","message":"Root cause: ZYNTAX_GC_EXPLAIN (with weak values now reported) shows the value held by one word of HirInterpreter::run_frame's own Rust frame, 0x4d8 above its stack pointer at the call into collectgarbage: a 16-byte ZyntaxValue temporary the dispatch loop reuses across ops (str q0, [sp, #0x4d0]), still holding the last table moved through it. Whether a later op overwrites it before the collection depends on how rustc lays out run_frame, which any change to the crate can shift; 63f980f9 changed only the layout. Clearing the native-call argument and result buffers does not help. A sound fix: while an interpreted frame is inside a call, its live values are rooted precisely through its register file and the call's read set, so the collector can skip that frame's Rust stack from the point control leaves (marked at each transfer, not at the start of the op, so a box made while marshalling is never hidden) up to the frame's top.","files":null}]}